          evolution: "The game evolved to have 'stackable' penalties, where multiple 2s played in sequence can force a player to draw 4, 6, or more cards. The 'Last Card' announcement rule was formalized to prevent players from sneaking out a win.",
          cultural: "In New Zealand, it is almost exclusively known as 'Last Card' and is a staple of school lunch breaks and family gatherings. The game serves as an introduction to card games for many children due to its simple rules and exciting special cards.",
